abstract: >-
  This is a lesson developed for participants who want to 
continue learning about Git after taking the official Carpentries
Version Control with Git lesson. This lesson will get participants
comfortable with creating branches in local and remote repositories,
and generally managing references in Git. This lesson has been 
developed for the Oregon State University Libraries Workshop Series.
This lesson uses the Carpentries template, and has been developed using these resources:
(1) The Git novece lesson from software carpentry, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.57467
(2) Lecture 6: Version Control (git) (2020) by Anish Athalye, taught as part of an MIT 
Computer Science class. https://missing.csail.mit.edu/2020/version-control/ 
(3) A lesson created at OSU by Ryan Wick, Clara Llebot and Steve Van Tuyl, 
using the software carpentry model https://github.com/osulp/git-advanced
